  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "Wall to wall – turn and carry it over the line",
  "description": "Four cones make a box of about 5 × 5 metres. Two players meet 1v1 inside the box, and each has their own goal line – an imaginary line between two of the cones. Whoever has the ball tries to turn away from the opponent and carry the ball over their line. If the opponent wins the ball, they attack their own line instead.\n\nPlay about a minute at a time and change opponents if a game is uneven. Set up several boxes side by side so everyone plays at once. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Turn with your body between the opponent and the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "What is your favourite way to turn with the ball?"
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Defender: when is it hardest to take the ball from someone turning?"
    }
  ],
